\f4\b\fs36 \cf0 Detecting network drives\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f3\b0\fs26 \cf0 diskutil
\f2\fs24  
\f4\b does not know about network shares
\f2\b0  (SMB, AFP, NFS, WebDAV). Those are mounted by the operating system rather than appearing as block devices.\
To detect them, you can use:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f3\fs26 \cf0 let mounts = run "mount" ""\
\
mounts.Split('\\n')\
|> Array.filter(fun line ->\
    line.Contains("smbfs") ||\
    line.Contains("nfs") ||\
    line.Contains("webdav") ||\
    line.Contains("afpfs"))\
|> Array.iter(printfn "%s")\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs24 \cf0 This will produce output such as:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f3\fs26 \cf0 server:/Projects on /Volumes/Projects (nfs)\
smb://NAS/Documents on /Volumes/Documents (smbfs)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

