\f4\b\fs36 \cf0 A more robust design\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs24 \cf0 If you\'92re planning to build a reusable tool (or eventually an F# library), I\'92d model the data like this:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f3\fs26 \cf0 type ConnectionType =\
    | Internal\
    | USB\
    | Thunderbolt\
    | SATA\
    | NVMe\
    | FireWire\
    | Network\
    | Virtual\
    | Unknown of string\
\
type Drive =\
    \{\
        DeviceIdentifier : string\
        VolumeName : string option\
        Size : int64\
        FileSystem : string option\
        Connection : ConnectionType\
        IsMounted : bool\
        IsInternal : bool\
        IsSSD : bool\
        IsReadOnly : bool\
        IsRemovable : bool\
        Manufacturer : string option\
        SerialNumber : string option\
    \}\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs24 \cf0 This makes it straightforward to:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Export to CSV or JSON.\
\ls3\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Filter by connection type (e.g., all USB or Thunderbolt drives).\
